This week has been off to a much better start =F0=9F=98=81 I'm pretty much =
feeling
back to normal, and Elder Warnick is feeling better too.

Monday

Tuesday
Today we had in person DCM, which was pretty fun. Afterwards we all got
Indo Curry together, and one of the senior missionaries, Elder McArthur
paid for everyone! =F0=9F=91=80 After Elder Warnick and I got back to Gobo =
we tried a
bit of finding and managed to make friends with a high schooler who is
insane at one arcade game. We couldn't exchange info (besides giving him
our number and telling him where the church is) but when we meet again
hopefully we will have our game night Flyer ready to pass to him! His name
was Yuuto. He also went to a Christian day care as a kid, and he has a good
view of the church I think. I'm glad we met him! We also went to visit a
store that a past friend owns to introduce ourselves. The owner is really
chill, and we were able to talk with him and his wife. I'm hoping we can go
back soon for a little tour of their workshop!

Wednesday
Today we got up early to head to Zone conference, and had a great time in
Abeno!! It was a pretty cool Zone conference compared to normal I think; I
feel like I learned a lot about the spirit, and how important it plays a
role in teaching and finding our friends. After getting home from Zone
conference we had Eikaiwa! A new person came too! Her name is Sachiko, and
she was invited by another Eikaiwa member =F0=9F=98=84 good day =E2=9C=A8=
=EF=B8=8F

Thursday
Today we actually taught Eikaiwa at a high school in Gobo! It was pretty
fun, but stressful. One of the teachers wants us to make sure more
missionaries can join us next time so we can participate more evenly with
the students. After that, we visited a guy named Mori, and our friend
Hatsue san. We talked with her for a while, and talked a lot about the
resurrection and afterlife. We were just talking on the doorstep, but her
husband pulled up, so we went inside and talked over some yuzu-tea for a
little while. We sent her a chapter from the Book of Mormon to read, and
she read it twice like immediately after the message, and shared her
thoughts with us. She doesn't necessarily believe in everything the way
it's written in the Book of Mormon right now, but I feel like she's really
progressing!

Friday
Today we talked with a lady at a stationery store and I made her some quick
art. Afterwards we went to a bunch of community centers trying to get
information about events we can join to get to know the people in Gobo and
hopefully make new friends! Good day for gathering info =F0=9F=98=8E

Saturday
Today we traveled to Tanabe, which was my first time! It's a bigger city in
our area that's a 40 minute train ride away from Gobo. We met up with
Brother and Sister Enomoto, and we got to have food at one of his friends'
restaurants. I made some art for his friend and signed it "from the
missionaries" haha. Afterwards we got dropped off at a nearby shopping mall
and talked with a group of like 4 teenagers and got a couple pictures with
them! I challenged them to talk with the missionaries next time they see
some! I also made some art for them, and I was requested to draw the logo
of a casino =F0=9F=98=82 I told them to avoid going there if they can lol. =
Later when
we got back to Gobo, we had Game night at the church. Sachiko came, and
even brought her 18 year old niece! We played ping pong all together and it
was hilarious =F0=9F=98=82 Sachiko faced off against Elder Warnick and beat=
 him 2-1
with plenty of slams =F0=9F=98=82 She's so funny. It's really cool how far =
one
connection with a person can go!

Sunday
Today was an awesome Sunday! I got to meet our newly baptized member Harold
for the first time. (He's been in the Philippines until now) He's very
chill and laid back. His Japanese still needs some work so I'm interpreting
again =F0=9F=92=AB=F0=9F=92=AB=F0=9F=98=B5=F0=9F=98=B5 It's worth the bless=
ings but it's exhausting =F0=9F=98=85 I need to up
my Japanese study. Today, a random Filipino lady named Sister Nikki also
showed up! She works on a cruise ship, and was stopped nearby so she came
to church. (I interpreted for her too) And to top things off, Sachiko san
came to church! She said she had work so she couldn't make it, but she came
during her break to Sacrament meeting! It was such a cool surprise =F0=9F=
=98=AE She
had to leave early too, but she was really enjoying the talks. It was so
cooool! Looking forward to seeing her again on Wednesday!

Monday
Today for Pday Elder Warnick and I traveled to Tanabe again and traveled to
a bunch of fun stores. My favorite was this thrift/antique shop; I got cool
CDs and a Japanese card game! Before all that though, we met wuth brother
Enomoto and helped trim some trees in front of the Tanabe church building.
Afterwards we went and got Sushi together! At one of the stores Elder
Warnick and I spent like 15 bucks trying to get some Magic cards from a
"stop the light" game and it was rigged and we didn't get anything =F0=9F=
=98=85=F0=9F=98=85
Elder Warnick felt sick and says he'll never waste money like that again
but he's glad that he learned his lesson lol. Me too! =F0=9F=98=82 Another =
cool thing
from today! We met Jian on the train, and got a time set up with him to
meet!! Lit!

All in all, it's been a pretty solid week, but we were only in Gobo for
half of it! This next week I'm excited to see what miracles we can
experience. It'll be Elder Warnicks last full week in Gobo (we both talked
with President Sano during our interviews so we know Elder Warnick is
leaving), so we gotta make sure it's a good one.

I love you guys so much, seriously. I have so many cool friends and loved
ones on my email list, every one of you are special to me. Please trust
that your trials are temporary, and place your trust in God! He will help
you to find comfort!

Love you!

--000000000000a0ec650648ba92f8
